// ── THE FROZEN RUNTIME-IDENTITY RESIDUAL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// WHAT THE DERIVATION DOES NOT REPRODUCE. Five producers of the deleted hand roster are called only
// with arguments that are values computed inside the claim (a serialized node, a grammar row), so
// every one of their call sites observes as `ArgumentNotClosedConstant` and the fold above can
// neither prove nor refute that two claims demand one identity. The recurrence is real -- the
// same script statements and grammar rows are demanded by many claims -- but it is a fact about
// runtime argument values, and no argument row is fixed before the claim runs.
//
// DISPOSITION (sharp-raven-357, 2026-10-03): kept as a FROZEN residual, DESIGN section 3's
// frozen-X carve-out -- no Y can hold this boundary yet, so X stays and takes no new rows. The
// population is CLOSED: the members are the arms of `FrozenRuntimeIdentityProducer`, the data row
// is derived from every arm, and the witness joins it by identity, so a sixth member is a refusal
// rather than an append. A producer with non-closed arguments that is NOT one of these is counted
// with its cause and never admitted.
//
// PURITY IS UNCHANGED BY THIS ROW. Admission here says only that the tier MAY retain the
// producer's fills. Every fill is still keyed by the resolved declaration AND the full argument
// row, and a hit is served only after the stored argument preimage is compared equal to the
// caller's (std.computation_identity; the hand roster served these the same way -- keyed by
// declaration and arguments, never by name alone).
//
// TRIGGER (the capability, DESIGN section 4b(3)): per-call runtime-argument demand identity
// available to .dag (demand-engine M1.b). With it the observation carries these sites' identities
// like any closed site, the fold decides them, and this residual is deleted whole.
type FrozenRuntimeIdentityProducer
  = BashFoldSerializeNode
  | BashFoldRelationRowWitness
  | GrammarRelationRowForEmitted
  | FormalProductionsFromCatalogNode
  | TargetProjectArrowBodyToValueExpression

type RuntimeIdentityShareRow {
  member: FrozenRuntimeIdentityProducer
  producer: String
  cause: CallSiteDemandCause
}

fn frozen_runtime_identity_producer_declaration(member: FrozenRuntimeIdentityProducer) -> String {
  match member {
    BashFoldSerializeNode => "v2.workflow.bash_command_fold_serialize.bash_fold_serialize_node"
    BashFoldRelationRowWitness => "v2.extdeps.languages.bash_command_fold.bash_fold_relation_row_witness"
    GrammarRelationRowForEmitted => "v2.compiler.target_serialize.grammar_relation_row_for_emitted"
    FormalProductionsFromCatalogNode => "v2.std.grammar.formal_productions_from_catalog_node"
    TargetProjectArrowBodyToValueExpression => "v2.std.compilers.target_model.target_project_arrow_body_to_value_expression"
  }
}

fn runtime_identity_share_row(member: FrozenRuntimeIdentityProducer) -> RuntimeIdentityShareRow {
  RuntimeIdentityShareRow {
    member: member,
    producer: frozen_runtime_identity_producer_declaration(member: member),
    cause: ArgumentNotClosedConstant
  }
}

data floor_cross_claim_runtime_identity_residual: List<RuntimeIdentityShareRow> = [
  runtime_identity_share_row(member: BashFoldSerializeNode),
  runtime_identity_share_row(member: BashFoldRelationRowWitness),
  runtime_identity_share_row(member: GrammarRelationRowForEmitted),
  runtime_identity_share_row(member: FormalProductionsFromCatalogNode),
  runtime_identity_share_row(member: TargetProjectArrowBodyToValueExpression)
]

fn runtime_identity_residual_producers(rows: List<RuntimeIdentityShareRow>) -> List<String> {
  list_map(xs: rows, f: fn(r) { r.producer })
}

fn floor_cross_claim_runtime_identity_residual_producers() -> List<String> {
  runtime_identity_residual_producers(rows: floor_cross_claim_runtime_identity_residual)
}

// ── REFUSED CANDIDATES: THE ROWS THIS ROSTER MEASURED AND TURNED DOWN ─────────────────────
//
// WHY A REFUSAL NEEDS A CARRIER AT ALL, and it is not tidiness. Until this type existed the file
// had three `List<String>` rosters for rows it ADMITS and nothing typed for a row it REFUSES, so
// every withdrawal had nowhere to go but prose and the header grew by one essay per negative
// result. That is not an authoring habit, it is a missing coproduct: a withdrawn candidate is a
// structured, recurring fact with an identity, a verdict, the claims the refusal was measured
// over, a citation, and a next trigger.
//
// AND THE PROSE COULD NOT DO THE JOB IT WAS DOING. DESIGN section 4c is explicit that semantic
// passes receive only the annotation-erased projection and that no `Accepted` program can read an
// annotation, so the paragraph that said it "stands in the withdrawn row's place so the next
// reader does not re-propose it" was asking a reader to do what no mechanism could. A paragraph
// stops nobody. A refused row, joined against the admitted rosters, refuses the re-proposal by
// execution.
//
// WHAT THESE ROWS DELIBERATELY DO NOT CARRY: the measurements. Not the normalised deltas, not the
// consumer-claim counts, not the per-identity cpu figures. DESIGN section 6 says to name the
// instrument and never transcribe its output, and moving seventy numbers out of an erased comment
// channel into typed fields would be transcription with a schema -- the same rot, now
// type-checked. `measurement` names the run pair and the artifact that re-derives the verdict;
// the numbers stay where they are produced.
// `KeyOmitsAnInputTheValueDependsOn` IS NOT A COST ARM AND MUST NOT BE FOLDED INTO ONE.
// `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` `refusal_names_a_comparison_and_prints_neither_side` states the
// rule this arm exists to obey: the other three arms all answer a COST question -- is serving
// cheaper than recomputing -- and filing a non-cost refusal under one of them is a MEANING FORK,
// because a cost refusal reads as "we measured and sharing lost" and ranks for a cost repair, while
// this one means SHARING IS NOT AVAILABLE AT ALL and ranks for a shape repair.
//
// THE DIFFERENCE IS BETWEEN "DO NOT BOTHER" AND "MUST NOT". A cost-refused row is legitimately
// re-proposable on new cost evidence; a row refused here may NOT come back on any amount of cost
// evidence, because the objection is that serving would be WRONG. The memo key is
// `(fn_node, args_hash)` and `args_hash` covers the DECLARED arguments only, so a producer whose
// value also depends on the resolving context can be served a value computed under a different
// context -- silently, with a plausible result. DESIGN section 5 puts that outside the ladder
// rather than low on it.
//
// `undeclared_input` NAMES WHAT THE KEY CANNOT SEE, so the row says which fact would have to become
// an argument -- or become part of the key -- for the refusal to end.
type ShareRefusalVerdict =
    MeasuredServeAboveRecompute
  | NoMeasuredEffectOverItsConsumers
  | SupersededBySingleAuthorityRepair { repaired_by: String }
  | KeyOmitsAnInputTheValueDependsOn { undeclared_input: String }

// `carrier_modules` is the set of consuming modules the refusal was MEASURED OVER -- the claims
// that carried it, read from the deciding run's own `[floor-shared-fill]` `modules=` field, which
// names the modules rather than counting them. It is descriptive at THIS grain and load-bearing
// at the ledger's: see the overlap note below `refused_row_carriers_transfer`.
type RefusedShareCandidate {
  producer: String
  verdict: ShareRefusalVerdict
  carrier_modules: List<String>
  measurement: String
  next_trigger: String
}

// ONE DECLARATION, TWO READERS. Both refused rows below ask the same question of the corpus, so it
// is answered once here rather than in a paragraph copied into each `measurement` string -- which is
// what an earlier revision did, and the copies could then drift apart on a one-line edit (DESIGN
// section 2).
//
// WHY THE ANNOTATION SAYS NO MORE THAN THAT: the declaration below IS prose, so an annotation
// restating its claims would be the same fork one level up, in the copy no consumer reads (DESIGN
// section 4c -- an annotation must not restate what the declaration structurally says). The grain,
// the frontier and the no-figure rule are stated once, in the string, where the rows actually read
// them. Found by review 65532.
fn homonym_census_note() -> String {
  "THE HOMONYM EVIDENCE IS CITED AT REFERENCE GRAIN AND IS A DECLARED FRONTIER. The refusal below fires on a bare spelling RESOLVED through a claim scope that carries two declarers, so the population that ranks this class is (referencing module, bare spelling, candidate declaring modules) -- not a count of homonymous DECLARATIONS, which is a different question a corpus can answer loudly while having no ambiguous reference at all. The reference-grain census is owned by `witty-otter-157` under the `swift-bat-902` reflection lane and is NOT YET AN ENTRY POINT; this row names no census symbol until it is, because a citation that resolves to nothing is worse than an admitted gap. NO CORPUS ROW RECORDS THIS POPULATION TODAY EITHER, AND AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS SENTENCE SAID ONE DID (review 65792). It cited `gunbc.bare_name_identity_consumer_census` as carrying a row sited at `v2.std.node_reflection` `resolve_type_node` with a `ReachabilityUnmeasured` reach. That row does not exist at this head -- every site in that roster is a v1 emitter module -- so the citation resolved to nothing, in the same sentence that calls a citation resolving to nothing worse than an admitted gap. It came from relaying a peer lane's description of its own UNLANDED PR as though it were a fact about the tree, which is the failure mode `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` `prose_repealed_by_the_change_that_wrote_it` names one step removed: not a claim this change falsified, but a claim no change had yet made true. The row and the reference-grain census are both PROPOSED in gunbc#11291 by `witty-otter-157` under the `swift-bat-902` reflection lane; neither has landed, and this row cites the symbol when one does. NO FIGURE IS CARRIED HERE IN EITHER DIRECTION (DESIGN section 6: name the instrument, never transcribe its output -- which governs a qualitative claim exactly as it governs a number). WHAT THE ANSWER WOULD MEAN, since that is what does not age: a NON-EMPTY reference population means the class has live specimens and the upstream repair ranks against a real one; an EMPTY population means these rows are UNGUARDED rather than harmful. NEITHER ANSWER CHANGES THE REFUSAL -- the census ranks the repair, it does not decide the enrolment, and a key that omits an input the value depends on may not be enrolled whatever the population is (DESIGN section 5: construction, not validation)."
}

